+## T28 — Membership integrity: no client-created or client-moved memberships
+Reasoning: Every members-only guarantee of this phase (typing topic, mentions, roster, read state, messages, 
attachments, receipts) trusts `conversation_members`; owner decision D9 puts the self-enrolment gap in scope.
+Task: No anon or authenticated client can create a `conversation_members` row, change a row's `conversation_id` or 
`user_id`, or gain membership of a conversation they were not given through any other client-reachable path (e.g. 
writing `conversations.participants`/`room_id` that the SECURITY DEFINER trigger `sync_conversation_members` syncs 
into memberships, other RPCs, views, or triggers); memberships keep being created by the existing server paths 
(conversation creation, room membership sync, seeding); a member's own preference fields (pin, star, archive, 
notifications, read cursor) keep working through the existing server routes; the inventory of client-reachable 
membership writers and the decision for each (closed, kept with reason) is recorded in TRACK.
+Done when: On the local database, a hostile authenticated user cannot become or appear as a member of a conversation 
they do not belong to by any client-reachable path in the inventory, and existing conversation creation, room 
conversations, preferences, archive, and read flows still work.
