36: ## T4 — Server-validated atomic mentions and current-member roster
37: Reasoning: Mentions are a data contract consumed by composer and notifications on both create paths; the 
autocomplete needs a current roster no existing read provides.
38: Task: A mention store holds application user IDs mentioned by a message, written in the same transaction as the 
first creation on both the text path and the attachment/voice path (since T3 every message insert — keyed, unkeyed, 
Phase 4 wrapper — runs inside `create_message_attempt`, and clients have no INSERT on public.messages), only for 
conversation members at that time other than the sender; requested mention IDs are part of the stored original 
composition (changed mentions on replay → 409; unchanged replay after a recipient left returns the stored message); 
only members can read mention records; no client can write them; messages fetched by members carry their mention IDs. 
An authorized read returns a conversation's current members (from `conversation_members`, so removed members are 
excluded) to members only.
39: Done when: The AC-024 server clauses, the AC-046 replay clause, and the roster contract hold on the local database 
for both create paths.
40: Verify by: Messaging DB integration tests: non-member and self IDs store nothing; changed-mention replay 409 with 
no change; forced mention-storage failure stores neither message, attachment links, nor mentions (text and attachment 
paths); anon/non-member read denied; direct client writes denied; unchanged replay after removal returns stored 
message; roster excludes a removed member and is denied to non-members; Phase 4/legacy compatibility passes; RLS 
review gate recorded.
41: Covers: FR-023, FR-024, BR-010, AC-024, AC-046, AC-035
42: Root: T4
